Subject: Default to system allocator under Fil-C
Policy-Class: P4-Audit
Rationale: Zend's 2 MiB chunk allocator hides intra-chunk overflows and UAF between PHP values; default USE_ZEND_ALLOC=0 under __FILC__ so every value gets its own capability.
Upstream-Status: Fil-C-Specific
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: 18e0199cef6c30fc815442c0dd3f9d97fae3702a
Origin-Kind: filc-upstream
Origin-Project: pizlonator/fil-c
Origin-Commit: 18e0199cef6c30fc815442c0dd3f9d97fae3702a
Origin-URL: https://github.com/pizlonator/fil-c/commit/18e0199cef6c30fc815442c0dd3f9d97fae3702a

diff --git a/Zend/zend_alloc.c b/Zend/zend_alloc.c
index c7babe1..0a70cdc 100644
--- a/Zend/zend_alloc.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_alloc.c
@@ -2731,7 +2731,13 @@ static void alloc_globals_ctor(zend_alloc_globals *alloc_globals TSRMLS_DC)
 {
 	char *tmp = getenv("USE_ZEND_ALLOC");
 
+#ifdef __FILC__
+	/* Default to system malloc so every PHP value gets its own capability.
+	 * Set USE_ZEND_ALLOC=1 to opt into Zend's chunk allocator. */
+	if (!tmp || !zend_atoi(tmp, 0)) {
+#else
 	if (tmp && !zend_atoi(tmp, 0)) {
+#endif
 		alloc_globals->mm_heap = malloc(sizeof(struct _zend_mm_heap));
 		memset(alloc_globals->mm_heap, 0, sizeof(struct _zend_mm_heap));
 		alloc_globals->mm_heap->use_zend_alloc = 0;
